From c2de0fc0ed2252de22064dc9e17e856d29013884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:14:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07214/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-33: larger-model
 g50t test -- parity not improvement, new truncation failure

REQ-32's option (b): does a larger model (Qwen3.6-27B-MTP, ~3x the frozen 9B live
generator) close g50t's content-accuracy ceiling? Same combined-fix config,
proposer swapped via explicit override to E3AgentPolicy (frozen _proposer()
production default untouched). Ran a fresh live episode, not a literal replay of
REQ-32's saved counterexample -- an honest scope departure, recorded rather than
glossed over.

First attempt (mtp=True) OOM'd -- self-draft loads the GGUF twice, ~32GB needed
for a 16GB file on a 24GB 3090. Independently rediscovered the same bug
REQ-ARC-WMTE-5596 already found and fixed in its own script one milestone
earlier; fixed here the same way (mtp=False).

Result: round 1 (induce) heldout_accuracy=0.125 -- parity with, not improvement
over, the 9B ceiling on this game, in contrast to REQ-ARC-WMTE-5596's own finding
that this same 27B candidate showed materially higher accuracy than the 9B
generator on two other games (m0r0 0.0->0.5, sk48 0.2->1.0). Round 2 (refactor)
then hit a new failure: proposer_ok=False, n_predict=4096 output limit -- the
same truncation class REQ-27/28/30 fixed for the 9B model, but that budget was
tuned against the 9B model only and doesn't carry over to a 3x larger model.

levels=0, no level-up, nothing banked. n=1 run/game/model-swap: does not prove
model scale is irrelevant to g50t (it demonstrably helped on other games), only
that it didn't help here -- the accuracy ceiling looks game-dependent, not a
uniform capability floor.

